- Include this license and retain existing copyright, attribution and third-party notices.
- Clearly identify material changes you make.
- Do not represent that recipients receive broader rights in the Licensors’ Software than this license permits.

Each recipient receives permission for the Licensors’ Software directly from the Licensors under this license. A recipient’s Commercial Use must qualify for its own trial or be covered by its own valid commercial license. Your trial or commercial license does not automatically extend to recipients.

The source-copying and source-sharing permissions in this section are available even if you work for a business, and continue after a commercial trial expires. They do not authorize running, deploying or making changes to the Software for Commercial Use beyond the applicable trial or commercial license. Nothing here limits rights that users independently have under GitHub’s applicable terms for viewing or forking a public repository.

You retain any rights you hold in your original modifications. Those rights do not remove the conditions applying to the Licensors’ Software contained in a modified version.

